tnotes":[{"year":null,"population_type":"STA","text":"The figure includes individuals recognised as stateless (refugees, asylum-seekers and not displaced persons) and individuals who filed a new application to request recognition as a stateless person and who are pending resolution.","view":"asylum"},{"year":null,"population_type":"STA","text":"Figure refers to a population of undetermined nationality.","view":"asylum"},{"year":2021,"population_type":"ASY","text":"The number of asylum applications includes 38,278 asylum applications not yet formalized, i.e. individuals with an appointment to complete the application procedure, as well as 11,066 applicants whose cases have been processed but have yet to receive notification of the decision on their asylum applications. The latter relate primarily to cases received prior to 2020. Until end-2020 these were reported under others of concern and have since been re-classified as asylum applications since the 2021 mid-year statistical report.","view":"asylum"},{"year":2022,"population_type":"ASY","text":"In 2022, Nicaraguans and Venezuelans (only October to December) started their applications by obtaining an appointment to formalize their asylum claim. The appointment process for Nicaraguans and Venezuelans ended in December 2022.","view":"asylum"}],"sources":["unhcr_countries","unhcr_population","unhcr_demographics","unhcr_idmc","unhcr_solutions","unhcr_asylum_applications","unhcr_footnotes","wpp_population","natural_earth"]}
